 "notes": "Rows 69v l.11-13 (segmenter l.12-14 of image 0084_0143) and 70r l.1-2 (image 0084_0144): 13 + 14 + 13 + 14 + 19 = 73, as the record; كوابل runs over the line end (3 + 2). Plain 1x / 0.85x line crops and 1.5x zooms. The text keyed is as enciphered: ادمعي -> مدمعي (the first sign is H, which is م in ودموعي, منهم, محمول and in this word; the clear text on 70r l.9 reads رضوا مدمعي), بهذا -> فهذا (the first sign is the same sweep as the ف of فرقادي; فهذا is also what the grammar wants after ان with a nominal answer; the clear text there is not clearly dotted). With the record wording the sweep would write ف and ب and H ا and م. Alif is the open hook (11), ya the er-loop (8), dal the horned triangle (7)."
